{
  "company_name": "DistroCapital Finance",
  "industry": "Industrial Distribution",
  "use_case": "Working capital and cash flow optimization for industrial distribution",
  "space_title": "DistroCapital Finance - Working Capital & Cash Flow 💰",
  "space_description": "**Scenario:** You sit in the treasury seat at DistroCapital Finance, steering working capital across 20 business units in 8 regions and segments from pipe & valve to electrical, welding, and corporate. Your cash conversion cycle is stuck in the 60-90 day band while best-in-class peers run under 45, and a handful of units are slipping toward Tight and Critical liquidity. Which business units are choking your cash conversion cycle, and where can you free up trapped working capital fastest?\n\n**Questions:**\n\n1. Showcase the different visualization options with interesting aspects of the dataset (agent)\n2. What is my current working capital composition by business segment and region, broken out by AR balance, inventory investment, and liquidity status? (agent)\n3. Which business segments have the highest cash conversion cycle and DSO, and where is the most net working capital tied up? (agent)",
