  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports Working Capital & Cash Flow Optimization for an industrial distributor with 20 business units across pipe & valve, industrial supply, electrical, welding, safety, corporate, and digital segments in 8 US regions. Stakeholders include the CFO (CCC, liquidity), Treasurer (cash position, forecast variance), AR Manager (DSO, collections), AP Manager (DPO, vendor terms), and Segment GMs (working-capital efficiency by BU).\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Cash Conversion Cycle = avg_ccc_days (cash_conversion_cycle_days); industrial distribution typical 60-90 days, best-in-class <45\n- DSO = avg_dso (dso_days on cash_transactions); B2B industrial target 30-45 days\n- DPO = dpo_days (cash_transactions); target 30-45 days; widen carefully to preserve supplier terms\n- Net cash flow = total_cash_inflow - total_cash_outflow (net_cash_flow measure)\n- Current ratio = avg_current_ratio; healthy 1.5-2.5x, <1.0 = liquidity warning\n- Net working capital (NWC) = ar_balance + inventory_investment - ap_balance (use the `net working capital USD` snippet)\n- Forecast variance = actual_cash_flow_usd - forecasted_cash_flow_usd (use the `cash flow variance` snippet)\n- Liquidity status = liquidity_status band (Strong / Adequate / Tight / Critical)\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - cashflow_monthly (source: business_units) — dims: txn_date, business_segment, region, payment_type; measures: total_cash_inflow, total_cash_outflow, total_ar_collected, net_cash_flow, transaction_count, unique_bu_count, max_cash_inflow.\n  - working_capital_monthly (source: working_capital_snapshots) — dims: forecast_month, business_segment, region, liquidity_status; measures: total_forecasted_cf, total_actual_cf, avg_ccc_days, avg_current_ratio, critical_count, unique_bu_count, max_forecasted_cash_flow.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. bu_id, bu_name, ar_balance_usd, ap_balance_usd, inventory_investment_usd, dso_days, dpo_days).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Showcase the different visualization options with interesting aspects of the dataset",
    "What is my current working capital composition by business segment and region, broken out by AR balance, inventory investment, and liquidity status?",
    "Which business segments have the highest cash conversion cycle and DSO, and where is the most net working capital tied up?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "What has been the peak cash_inflow each month?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT txn_date, MEASURE(max_cash_inflow) AS max_cash_inflow",
        "FROM {fqn}.cashflow_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY txn_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has total cash inflow trended over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT txn_date, MEASURE(total_cash_inflow) AS total_cash_inflow",
        "FROM {fqn}.cashflow_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY txn_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has critical count changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT forecast_month, MEASURE(critical_count) AS critical_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.working_capital_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY forecast_month"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has total cash inflow in trended over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT txn_date, SUM(cash_inflow_usd) AS total_cash_inflow_usd",
        "FROM {fqn}.business_units",
        "GROUP BY txn_date",
        "ORDER BY txn_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has total total ar balance trended over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, SUM(ar_balance_usd) AS total_ar_balance_usd",
        "FROM {fqn}.cash_transactions",
        "GROUP BY snapshot_date",
        "ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has the average current ratio (assets/liabilities) changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT forecast_month, AVG(current_ratio) AS avg_current_ratio",
        "FROM {fqn}.working_capital_snapshots",
        "GROUP BY forecast_month ORDER BY forecast_month"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How many distinct transactions appeared each month?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', txn_date) AS month, COUNT(DISTINCT transaction) AS distinct_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.business_units",
        "GROUP BY 1",
        "ORDER BY 1"
      ]
    }
